/-!
# projective submanifolds with Chow equations are smooth projective schemes

Source: `rmk:bdiv:L749` (algebraization of the book's blow-up models).

Let `Ψ : Y → ℙᴺ` be a holomorphic embedding of a compact complex manifold of dimension `n`, and
`P_k` homogeneous polynomials of degree `m` which generate the ideal sheaf of the affine cone over
`Ψ(Y)` off the vertex and cut out `Ψ(Y)` (Chow's theorem, `SGPT.GAGA.ChowBl.chow_image`).  Then the
projective scheme `V = Proj(ℂ[x]/(P_k))` (`BD5ProjScheme`) is smooth of relative dimension `n`
over `ℂ` (`zeroStructure_smoothOfRelativeDimension`).

Proof, at a complex point `q` of `V` over `p ∈ ℙᴺ(ℂ)`:
* analytically, `C = Ψ(Y)` (read in the native `ℙᴺ(ℂ)`) is regular of dimension `n` at `p`
  (`regularAtDim_of_immersion`) and its ideal is generated by the dehomogenized `P_k`
  (`vanishingIdeal_mem_iff_isInSpanAt_genFun`); `BD5LocalEquations` selects `c = N - n` of them,
  `g₁, …, g_c`, still generating, with independent differentials;
* algebraically, the kernel of the surjective stalk map `𝒪_{ℙᴺ,p} → 𝒪_{V,q}` contains the `g_j`, and
  every element of it has a germ vanishing on `C`, hence (faithful flatness of
  `𝒪_{ℙᴺ,p} → 𝒪^{an}_{ℙᴺ,p}`, `mem_ideal_iff_schemeNativeStalkGerm`) lies in `(g₁, …, g_c)`;
  the native directional derivations dual to the `dg_j` (`nativeStalkDerivation`) and the Jacobian
  criterion `BD5LocalSmooth` give formal smoothness and `dim Ω = N - c = n`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 1600000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

noncomputable section

namespace SGPT.BDivisor.BD5

